    <mxCell id="key" value="&lt;b&gt;Why three terminals&lt;/b&gt;   PASSED and FAILED are both complete scans; ERROR means the scan could not be completed. Collapsing ERROR into FAILED would let a partial scan look authoritative, which is the failure mode the report contract exists to prevent.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Re-baselining rule&lt;/b&gt;   the only legitimate way to move the expected hash is the Re-baselined path: block text and baseline file change in the same commit, change_reason is non-null, and the commit id is recorded. A hash change without that evidence is FAILED, not Re-baselined.&#10;&lt;b&gt;No terminal is sticky&lt;/b&gt;   nothing caches the verdict; every run recomputes from file bytes, so a stale green is impossible." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#999999;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="40" y="585" width="1090" height="95" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
